From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:55:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mark the double-quoted identifier check as used outside its
 assertion

ExceptionFormatValue::Format() calls HasDoubleQuotedIdentifier() only
inside D_ASSERT(), so in a release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to
nothing, the static function is never referenced and -Wunused-function
reports it as defined but not used. A (void) reference after the
assertion marks it used, the way the engine already treats locals that
only an assertion reads.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.
---
 src/duckdb/src/common/exception_format_value.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/common/exception_format_value.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/common/exception_format_value.cpp
index 5c797c0bb4..376d6934f5 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/common/exception_format_value.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/common/exception_format_value.cpp
@@ -126,6 +126,7 @@ static bool HasDoubleQuotedIdentifier(const string &msg, const std::vector<Excep
 string ExceptionFormatValue::Format(const string &msg, std::vector<ExceptionFormatValue> &values) {
 	// identifiers are quoted by the formatter, the format string must not quote them again
 	D_ASSERT(!HasDoubleQuotedIdentifier(msg, values));
+	(void)HasDoubleQuotedIdentifier;
 	try {
 		std::vector<duckdb_fmt::basic_format_arg<duckdb_fmt::printf_context>> format_args;
 		for (auto &val : values) {
